Parity disposition: the web <DatePresetChips> is a PURE presentational component (its only "hook" is
useTranslation; it takes presetIds/activeId/onSelect/size/ariaLabel as props and renders a row of <Button>
chips — no fetch, no React-Query, no Promise; its only side effect is resolving p.resolve() over new Date()
on tap). It therefore has NO loading / error / stale / offline branch. This surface reproduces the source's
REAL branches faithfully — the populated chip row, the active primary highlight (activeId), and the empty
row (presetIds → zero known presets, rendered as a labelled native empty state rather than a bare box) —
exactly as the in-tree sibling presentational primitive ActiveFilterChips (0147) documents and does.
Inventing fetch chrome would fabricate states the source does not have (Honesty Covenant #5 cuts both ways).
Charts/maps: none in source → none here.

